Validate AIC dynamic metadata before touching registers.

Resolve both AIC3 capability offsets before the first capability read, reject
failed/negative/unaligned offsets, and validate all external-interrupt records
before any configuration write. Read scalar ADT properties through an
exact-length wrapper before copying, keep the existing AIC2 fixed offsets, and
preserve public aic_init failure clearing. This validates source-level input
contracts only; it does not assign IRQ target semantics.

